[jon@bdmrrr.bdm.com (Jon Humphreys) writes:]
[] Why are people worried about nethack staying at medieval technology 
[] when the game already contains many items that are clearly modern

all things in moderation is the key (from my personal prespective).
typically dragons, dungeons and the like are drawn from medieval
settings. a few modern extras add spice, as you mention, and should
not overly detract from the focus of a medieval forum. when a concept
can be represented in two or more ways and one of those ways happens
to have a distinctly medieval flavor then i believe the game should
favor the medieval approach (for overall consistency). just my opinion.

